  'ethical-elephant-tour-and-pad-thai-cooking-in-chiang-mai': {
            averageRating: 4.95,
            totalReviews: 148,
            guideRating: 4.98,
            valueRating: 4.82,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Danielle", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-03", text: "So fun- our guide Adam was so lovely! He explained everything so well and it was just such a wonderful way to experience the elephants without infringing on their boundaries. So lovely- would highly recommend!!", photos: ["https://images.asiabylocals.com/asiabylocals/reviews/ethical-elephant-tour-and-pad-thai-cooking-in-chiang-mai/7924357/1600.webp", "https://images.asiabylocals.com/asiabylocals/reviews/ethical-elephant-tour-and-pad-thai-cooking-in-chiang-mai/7924360/1600.webp", "https://images.asiabylocals.com/asiabylocals/reviews/ethical-elephant-tour-and-pad-thai-cooking-in-chiang-mai/7924361/1600.webp"] },
                { author: "Elizabeth", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-16", text: "Wonderful experience! Learned a lot about each elephants history and the people who take care of them. Very ethical sanctuary!", photos: ["https://images.asiabylocals.com/asiabylocals/reviews/ethical-elephant-tour-and-pad-thai-cooking-in-chiang-mai/7592872/1600.webp"] },
                { author: "Victoria", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-27", text: "What an amazing and insightful experience. Everything was perfect from start to finish. Our guide, Adam is very experienced in working with elephants; he made the trip extremely informative and insightful. We prepared some food for the elephants which help with their digestion before leaving the food down and letting them eat it themselves. There was absolutely no touching of the elephants involved. The pad thai we prepared was also delicious! The guides really do have a love for these gentle creatures and it shows, their boundaries are respected and they are cared for. Would 100% recommend.", photos: ["https://images.asiabylocals.com/asiabylocals/reviews/ethical-elephant-tour-and-pad-thai-cooking-in-chiang-mai/6873459/1600.webp"] },
                { author: "Katerina", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-11", text: "We had an amazing day! Completely enjoyed by all three of us! The guides Mr Su and Miss Tukta were great! Informative and interesting and great to see the work everyone is doing at the sanctuary to help the elephants!" },
                { author: "Aimy", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-09", text: "Absolutely loved this tour! Our guide was so kind and knowledgeable, it was in an amazing coffee farm setting and the experience of roasting our own coffee beans to take away was so special. I loved learning about the processes of coffees, different roasts and aromas and I loved the overall experience. 10/10!" },
                { author: "Laceemai", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-07-11", text: "The most ethical sanctuary I have ever seen. The elephants were treated amazingly, I couldn’t recommend more definitely book this over other sanctuaries in the area" },
                { author: "Jennifer", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-18", text: "A very good morning, ethical and great value for money." },
                { author: "Russell", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-26", text: "Exactly what we expected and more. Elephants seemed happy in their surroundings. Guide was very good, informative and helpful. The food preparation and feeding without touching was very nice to see and taken part in. Our guide Tuck was a good teacher in the Pad Thai class at the end, and the food we cooked was excellent. Driver for the trip was very careful and attentive, unlike some we’ve had on other trips. The only slight downside was that it was quite hot in the van on the return journey, but I’m sure if we’d have asked the driver would have sorted it out for us. All in an excellent 2/3 of" },
                { author: "Dermorneay", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-20", text: "Such a lovely day with our guide Tuk Tuk 🐘🤍 She was so kind and knowledgeable, sharing so much about the elephants and making the whole experience feel really special. This sanctuary is truly ethical, which made it even more meaningful. It’s only been open around 8 months and already feels like such a beautiful, well-cared-for place. I’d 100% recommend visiting, and I can’t wait to come back again in the future 🙌🏾✨" },
                { author: "Vidar", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-18", text: "We had a great time at Big Boy Elephant! Even though no elephant was forced to do anything, we got up close and personal with the elephants. Pretty pricy considering that there is similar activities for half the price. The pad thai was amazing and all the guides were very friendly!" },
                { author: "Bella", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-16", text: "Was one best experiences I’ve ever done! Completely ethical, very educational. Everyone was so friendly and they made it easy for everyone to join in. Wor the very penny! (Special thanks to our driver, he made the trip)⭐️" },
                { author: "Jake", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-11", text: "Can’t imagine any place being better than this. I know people always say seeing elephants are amazing but it genuinely was thanks to Big Boy Sanctuary. No stress or harm caused, just observed them freely and can tell they’re being well looked after. Pickup was on time and everybody on site spoke perfect English. Hard to believe they put this much energy and enthusiasm into explaining the elephants lives every day. Big bonus and a lot of fun having the cooking class included, as well as making the elephants food. Only reason there aren’t a ton of reviews is because they’re newly opened." }
            ]
        },
