  'day-tour-to-pai-highlights-by-private-car-in-chiang-mai': {
            averageRating: 4.53,
            totalReviews: 36,
            guideRating: 4.64,
            valueRating: 4.23,
            reviews: [
                { author: "Amy", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-08-28", text: "Tiger was a great driver and really friendly. Although he could not speak much English he did use a translator app so it was not an issue. We were taken to all of the spots on the list and given free time to enjoy them all and could move on when we wanted to. We were never rushed at all. We actually finished the spots early so Tiger took us to a waterfall which was really beautiful. Each site was beautiful and so quiet it felt like we were alone at most of them." },
                { author: "Jaydon", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-02-15", text: "so much fun, amazing tour guide that was extremely patient and an incredible driver" },
                { author: "Elias", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-04-25", text: "Good experience, nice driver and scenic route. The curves didn’t bother us that much. It was off season so the area wasn’t as expected. Pai is famous for its rice fields but they we’re all dried out at this time of the year. But that was our fault not checking on that. :-) The monument bridge you could actually skip - not worth it. I would add the Bamboo bridge to that tour. Which must be a real highlight in rainy season." },
                { author: "Jasmine", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-02-09", text: "Our tour guide New was so friendly and informative - he spoke very good English and explained pretty well the history behind each spot. Most importantly - he’s such a pro and we ended up with so many beautiful pictures as though we had a photographer with us 🤩 He’s also very flexible in terms of itinerary; he brought us to two places that wasn’t on the itinerary - Huai Nam Dang National Park and Tha Pai Hot Spring - and both were fun and beautiful! We had to skip Yun Lai and Pai Walking Street because of the timing (both are more available from evening onwards but we had to depart from Pai by" },
                { author: "Belinda", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2025-01-21", text: "We had a great day with Korn as our driver and guide. Our base was in Chiang Mai, Thailand. He picked us up from our hotel and drove us 3 hours each way to a mountain village called Pai. He stopped at a few great sites on the way there and back. Korn spoke a reasonable amount of English, was informative, friendly, and caring. He was very attentive to my elderly aunt which freed my husband and me to head off at a good pace at the various sites. The drive to Pai is very steep and winding but Korn drove very carefully the entire day and we felt safe at all times despite the other crazy drivers on" },
                { author: "Koh", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2024-12-26", text: "Driver Tiger is very experienced and good. Though he doesn't speak English can feel his sincerity and he is always smiling" },
                { author: "Eduardo", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 4, date: "2025-03-19", text: "The driver guide was punctual and we were dropped in all the pkaces that were inckuded in the itinerary. We liked that she was eager to take our group photos. We just thought that tbat car couldd have been kept in a more tidy condition. Overall, it was a good service." },
                { author: "tom", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 3, date: "2026-05-28", text: "De plekken die je bezoekt zijn mooi en dit is zeker een fijne oplossing als je niet in Pai wilt slapen. Echter sprak onze driver vrijwel geen Engels en brengt je alleen naar de plekken toe zonder enige informatie. Achteraf is het de 160 euro in totaal zeker niet waard, aangezien er ook niet eens eten en drinken bij zit. Je kunt beter een Grab driver van de straat plukken en hem vragen of hij je voor 50 euro rond wilt rijden." },
                { author: "Paty", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-05-26", text: "Tomo unas fotos increíbles" },
                { author: "Giuseppe", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-10", text: "Bellissima la driver Chao ( spero aver scritto bene il suo nome)è stata cortesissima e disponibile ha guidato benissimo nelle tante curve da Chiang Mai a Pai e viceversa e abbiamo avuto tutto il tempo per visitare le attrazioni previste anzi abbiamo anche visitato il Karen village consigliatissima" },
                { author: "Kerstin", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 5, date: "2026-03-07", text: "Entspannte Tour mit sehr umsichtiger Fahrerin. Viel vom Norden Thailands entdeckt, individuelle Absprachen sehr gut 👍" },
                { author: "Traveller", country: "Verified traveller review", rating: 4, date: "2026-02-10", text: "Der Canyon war super schön, die anderen Stopps nichts besonderes aber generell hat uns Pai gut gefallen. Es war nicht wirklich guided da unsere Fahrerin uns eigentlich nur abgesetzt hat und wir uns nach einer Zeit wieder am Auto getroffen haben. Insgesamt fanden wir es zu teuer" }
            ]
        },
